Standards-Version: 1.0.0

Package: sonic-thermalctld-rs
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, python3, sonic-platform-common
Description: SONiC thermal control daemon, in Rust
 Rust port of thermalctld.  It reaches the platform through the generated
 cross-language facade in sonic-platform-common, which calls whichever
 vendor's Python sonic_platform package the image installs -- so this one
 binary runs on any platform that has one, and no vendor has to change
 anything to get it.
 .
 Writes the same TEMPERATURE_INFO, FAN_INFO, FAN_DRAWER_INFO and
 PHYSICAL_ENTITY_INFO entries to STATE_DB as the Python implementation; the
 two are compared field for field by the differential test.
 .
 The binary embeds a CPython interpreter to make those calls.  A later phase
 replaces the bridge with a native Rust implementation of the same trait,
 which removes the interpreter without touching the daemon.
